# firewall1: a chain that is never called
#
# nftables basics: a TABLE (with a family: ip, ip6, inet = both, arp,
# bridge, netdev) holds CHAINS, chains hold RULES, evaluated top to bottom
# until one gives a verdict (accept, drop, reject, jump...).
#
# A chain only sees packets if it is a BASE chain, one attached to a netfilter
# hook:
#     type filter hook input priority filter; policy drop;
# Without that line it is a "regular" chain, which only runs when another
# rule jumps to it. It loads without complaint and does nothing at all.
#
# The check loads this into server b (10.0.0.2) with `nft -f`, which runs
# ssh-like (22), http (80) and 8080 services, and tests from a (10.0.0.1):
#     port 22 open, ping answered, ports 80 and 8080 closed
#
# Your task: make this chain actually filter incoming traffic, dropping
# everything not explicitly accepted. Right now everything gets through.
#
#   netlings sandbox firewall1   then   ip netns exec b nft -f ruleset.nft
#                                       ip netns exec b nft list ruleset

flush ruleset

table inet filter {
  chain input {
    iif lo accept
    ct state established,related accept
    tcp dport 22 accept
    icmp type echo-request accept
    drop
  }
}
